      "why_it_matters": "A test-inbox demo already introduces transport credentials, allowlisting, synthetic substitution, recipient-set exclusion, and a hard send cap. Combining it with Asynq adds at-least-once delivery, retries, worker crashes, duplicate execution, and durable idempotency. The requirement for test delivery to occur at most once across those events is a separate delivery-safety product surface, not a minimal demonstration of either capability.",
