      "autofix_class": "manual",
      "suggested_fix": "Replace R17's opening obligation with: \"The optional Asynq demonstration may enqueue a bounded fixture and wait for worker completion within one invocation. It must report enqueue and task outcomes, but it need not provide durable campaign recovery, post-terminal cancellation fencing, or a separate campaign lifecycle model. If Redis or terminal evidence becomes unavailable before the bounded demo completes, the command reports failure or limited trust and does not claim completion.\" Remove the requirements in AE19 for intentionally preserving acknowledged work and in AE20 for making delayed redelivery inert after a terminal report. Keep cancellation semantics only in the required local path under R10.",
